----------------------------------------

Standard Python/Flask Ignore List

----------------------------------------

Byte-compiled / optimized / dynamically generated files

pycache/
*.pyc
*$py.class
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.dmypy.json

Environment

Ignore the virtual environment folder entirely

/venv/
/env/

Specific file created by venv and pipenv

pip-log.txt
pip-selfcheck.json
.python-version

IDE and Editor Files

VS Code

.vscode/

Sublime Text

*.sublime-workspace

Atom

.atom/

----------------------------------------

Project-Specific Ignore List

----------------------------------------

Database Files

Although 'leave.db' is small, it's often best practice to ignore the

local development database and let the deploy script create an empty one.

For now, since you might be collaborating, you might keep it, but generally ignore:

/leave.db

Sensitive/Local Config Files (CRUCIAL for real-world apps)

If you stored API keys or sensitive settings in a local file:

.env

instance/

config.py # (if it contains secrets)

Log files

*.log
tmp/